    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Source datasets:\nFoxDen lake: Meteorological data was not available at FoxDen pond/lake. Instead, data from the National Weather Service station at Kotzebue, AK (~90km ENE, citation) was used and solar radiation was obtained from NASA CERES.\nAtqasuk lake: The meteorological data for the Atqasuk lake comes from two sources: the South Meade site is the United States Geological Survey (USGS) meteorological station and the Atqasuk lake meteorological station from the Circumarctic Lakes Observation Network (CALON). The meteorological data includes: pressures [mb], rain [mm], air temperature [C], wind speed [m/s], gust speed [m/s], wind direction, and solar radiation [W/m].\nToolik lake: The meteorological data is collected at the nearby Toolik Field Station (~30m W, citation) and includes atmospheric air pressure [mb], all season precipitation [mm], snow depth [m], air temperature [C], wind speed [m/s], wind direction [degrees], and solar radiation [W/m].\nAll input datasets were visually inspected and do not have any missing values or outliers that can affect the LAKE2.0 model performance. More information on the data pre-/post-processing can be found in Clark et al., (in prep)."
    ],
